@startuml
title III-01 - Customer account registration

autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Customer
boundary "Customer Portal" as Web
control "Account API" as API
database "CRM Database" as DB

Customer -> Web: Enter registration form
Web -> API: POST /api/auth/register
API -> API: Validate required fields,\nemail format and password policy

alt Invalid input
    API --> Web: 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
    Web --> Customer: Show field errors
else Valid input
    API -> API: Hash password with BCrypt
    API -> DB: INSERT user

    alt Duplicate email constraint violation
        DB --> API: UNIQUE(email) violation
        API --> Web: 409 EMAIL_ALREADY_EXISTS
        Web --> Customer: Show email already registered
    else User created
        DB --> API: User created
        API --> Web: 201 Created
        Web --> Customer: Show registration success
    end
end

note over API,DB
  UNIQUE(email) is the concurrency guard.
  Do not rely on a check-before-insert query alone.
end note

@enduml
